WEBVTT

1
00:01:11.132 --> 00:01:16.132
Subtitles by explosiveskull

2
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.265
<i>The leaders come
off turn two</i>

3
00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.570
<i>with only three laps to go.</i>

4
00:01:22.871 --> 00:01:25.537
<i>Bob Linsky in the white
number 33 car has a razor-thin</i>

5
00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:28.676
<i>lead over Cam Munroe
in midnight blue number two.</i>

6
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.780
<i>These two
have been scrapping it out</i>

7
00:01:33.782 --> 00:01:36.716
<i>all season long here in
super late model race.</i>

8
00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:37.884
<i>They sure have, Jimmy.</i>

9
00:01:37.886 --> 00:01:40.453
<i>Cam Munroe drives
for his dad and crew chief,</i>

10
00:01:40.455 --> 00:01:43.191
<i>local racing legend,
Sam "The Man" Munroe.</i>

11
00:01:46.762 --> 00:01:50.364
<i>He might be the best dirt
track racer I've ever seen.</i>

12
00:01:59.508 --> 00:02:02.509
<i>And hold on right there!
Cam Munroe dives inside</i>

13
00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:04.279
<i>with a slick pass on Linsky.</i>

14
00:02:04.513 --> 00:02:05.679
- <i>He's done it!</i>
- Yeah!

15
00:02:05.681 --> 00:02:07.614
<i>Straight up
amazing driving.</i>

16
00:02:07.616 --> 00:02:08.550
Yes!

17
00:02:09.852 --> 00:02:11.786
<i>This race is
coming right down to the wire</i>

18
00:02:11.788 --> 00:02:14.255
<i>here at Talladega,
with only one lap to go.</i>

19
00:02:14.523 --> 00:02:17.256
<i>We might be seeing a changing
of the guard right here</i>

20
00:02:17.258 --> 00:02:19.661
<i>with young Cam Munroe
in the lead.</i>

21
00:02:20.729 --> 00:02:22.731
<i>Can he hold onto the win?</i>

22
00:02:27.669 --> 00:02:29.335
<i>Oh! Oh, no, no, no!</i>

23
00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:30.336
<i>Smoke from under the hood</i>

24
00:02:30.338 --> 00:02:32.441
<i>of the number two car
of Cam Munroe.</i>

25
00:02:36.411 --> 00:02:38.878
<i>Whoa! Big problems rumbling
here for Team Munroe.</i>

26
00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.847
<i>That engine's been
a problem all season.</i>

27
00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:44.018
<i>And there goes
Bob Linsky ripping past</i>

28
00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.220
<i>Cam Munroe.</i>

29
00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:47.054
<i>Looks like
Cam Munroe is gonna be</i>

30
00:02:47.056 --> 00:02:48.321
<i>a bridesmaid here tonight.</i>

31
00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:52.360
<i>His car dying completely
just shy of the finish line.</i>

32
00:02:55.064 --> 00:02:56.363
<i>The checkered flag goes up</i>

33
00:02:56.365 --> 00:03:00.433
<i>for Bob "Lead Foot" Linsky,
who clinches the championship</i>

34
00:03:00.435 --> 00:03:04.473
<i>with this win, making it three
titles in a row for Linsky.</i>

35
00:03:05.674 --> 00:03:08.843
<i>Well, Jimmy,
racing has a heck of a lot</i>

36
00:03:08.845 --> 00:03:11.679
<i>to do with the driver,
but you gotta have the car</i>

37
00:03:11.681 --> 00:03:13.013
<i>to back it up on the track.</i>

38
00:03:13.015 --> 00:03:15.616
<i>Yeah. The Munroe
car is fast when it runs,</i>

39
00:03:15.618 --> 00:03:18.052
<i>but it's been plagued by engine
problems all season,</i>

40
00:03:18.054 --> 00:03:21.990
<i>and there's definitely no love
lost between Sam Munroe</i>

41
00:03:21.992 --> 00:03:22.958
<i>and Bob Linsky.</i>

42
00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.860
<i>For sure.</i>

43
00:03:25.061 --> 00:03:27.094
<i>I know Cam Munroe will be back
next season, but right now</i>

44
00:03:27.096 --> 00:03:29.663
<i>it's Bob Linsky's moment in
the sun as he takes</i>

45
00:03:29.665 --> 00:03:32.433
<i>his victory lap, and the fans
here at Talladega</i>

46
00:03:32.435 --> 00:03:34.904
<i>let him know
they appreciate his win.</i>

47
00:04:14.911 --> 00:04:16.512
What a good day for you.

48
00:04:18.381 --> 00:04:21.852
David, do you mind helping
Cam load up his car?

49
00:04:22.552 --> 00:04:23.720
I gotta go to work.

50
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:30.394
Super!

51
00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:32.963
All right.

52
00:04:37.935 --> 00:04:38.869
Whoo!

53
00:05:18.977 --> 00:05:20.544
We're ready for you.

54
00:06:12.964 --> 00:06:14.098
<i>Pick your weapon.</i>

55
00:06:14.498 --> 00:06:17.602
- Uh... Gold.
- Gold, all right.

56
00:06:18.136 --> 00:06:19.068
Bait your hook.

57
00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.170
I'm not gonna have
to touch a worm, am I?

58
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:24.642
Hell no! I don't use worms,
I use hot dogs.

59
00:06:25.743 --> 00:06:28.045
- Pinch a little off like that.
- Okay.

60
00:06:28.047 --> 00:06:31.114
And we take our hook, you gotta
be careful with the hook,

61
00:06:31.116 --> 00:06:33.183
and we just hook it on real good

62
00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:35.818
so it doesn't fall off.
All right.

63
00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.188
Now, stand up.

64
00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.791
Now, I'm gonna come
and reach around you like this.

65
00:06:41.793 --> 00:06:44.163
- Mm-hm.
- I like this part.

66
00:06:46.931 --> 00:06:49.767
Now, seriously, why did you
move down here?

67
00:06:49.969 --> 00:06:52.171
- After the divorce...
- Yeah.

68
00:06:52.838 --> 00:06:56.507
...I just... I just needed to
get away from Steve and...

69
00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.710
and everything that reminded me
of our life together, you know?

70
00:07:00.712 --> 00:07:02.947
- Mm-hm.
- When I got offered

71
00:07:03.781 --> 00:07:05.815
the teaching job
at a reasonable salary

72
00:07:05.817 --> 00:07:11.023
in this quaint little town,
I jumped at the chance.

73
00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.558
Well, I sure am glad you did.

74
00:07:14.593 --> 00:07:15.627
Yeah, me too.

75
00:07:17.997 --> 00:07:19.598
I opened up. What about you?

76
00:07:20.733 --> 00:07:21.934
Mm-hm.

77
00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.869
We don't have
to talk about that.

78
00:07:26.871 --> 00:07:29.274
No. it's all right.
You're right.

79
00:07:29.808 --> 00:07:31.977
You told me your story.
Why can't I tell you mine?

80
00:07:32.878 --> 00:07:35.714
Um... Jen and I,
we grew up together,

81
00:07:36.148 --> 00:07:38.217
and she was
the first girl I kissed.

82
00:07:39.952 --> 00:07:42.122
You know, we always knew
we were gonna get married,

83
00:07:43.223 --> 00:07:47.526
and... she saw something
in me that nobody else did,

84
00:07:47.993 --> 00:07:50.827
including my father.
I mean, I felt like

85
00:07:50.829 --> 00:07:55.000
I could win races
and bag trophies, and...

86
00:07:55.768 --> 00:07:57.002
and I did for a while.

87
00:08:01.307 --> 00:08:02.308
What happened?

88
00:08:04.177 --> 00:08:07.080
Well, she... she died and...
and, uh, it was, uh,

89
00:08:07.781 --> 00:08:10.014
- it was in a car accident.
- I'm sorry.

90
00:08:10.016 --> 00:08:11.017
No, no, no.

91
00:08:11.984 --> 00:08:13.152
It's a part of me, you know.

92
00:08:15.921 --> 00:08:17.621
I don't know why,
I just thought of this.

93
00:08:17.623 --> 00:08:18.857
When I was senior
in high school,

94
00:08:20.126 --> 00:08:23.860
my friend Stumpy and I, we got
kicked out of school for doing

95
00:08:23.862 --> 00:08:25.298
donuts in the parking lot.

96
00:08:26.099 --> 00:08:28.802
And, uh, it was my dad's
'64 Galaxy.

97
00:08:29.335 --> 00:08:31.636
And, uh... Just 'cause you

98
00:08:31.638 --> 00:08:33.171
talked about school,
or it just stirred up

99
00:08:33.173 --> 00:08:35.175
- a school memory or something.
- What are donuts?

100
00:08:36.975 --> 00:08:38.811
Mm.

101
00:08:44.818 --> 00:08:48.352
You like it? I've never done
one before.

102
00:08:48.354 --> 00:08:50.924
- Oh!
- This is my first time.

103
00:08:51.124 --> 00:08:52.424
Oh, great!

104
00:09:07.974 --> 00:09:09.042
Hey, champ!

105
00:09:10.143 --> 00:09:11.678
Is that supposed to be funny?

106
00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.648
Depends on how you
look at it, I guess.

107
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.318
I could see you're all
pissed off,

108
00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.654
and I guess I would be too
if I was you.

109
00:09:21.922 --> 00:09:22.890
What's that supposed to mean?

110
00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.692
It just means that you got
a whole bunch of talent, son...

111
00:09:26.826 --> 00:09:28.161
but it ain't gonna do
you no good

112
00:09:28.428 --> 00:09:30.029
'cause you got
horseshit equipment.

113
00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.963
Is there any point to this
conversation,

114
00:09:31.965 --> 00:09:33.465
or do you just like
to hear yourself talk?

115
00:09:33.467 --> 00:09:34.667
I'm just trying to help.

116
00:09:37.837 --> 00:09:39.073
Come on up and talk to me.

117
00:09:39.772 --> 00:09:42.007
Just man to man.
We'll have a chat. No big deal,

118
00:09:42.009 --> 00:09:43.210
no pressure. No nothing.

119
00:09:45.112 --> 00:09:46.247
No harm in listening.

120
00:09:47.381 --> 00:09:49.816
I'm your friend,
don't forget it.

121
00:10:01.395 --> 00:10:03.996
- Tell me about your hobby.
- Hobby?

122
00:10:03.998 --> 00:10:07.735
- Yeah, racing.
- Hell no.

123
00:10:08.836 --> 00:10:10.070
Racing ain't no hobby.

124
00:10:11.505 --> 00:10:14.273
It's more like
a family tradition.

125
00:10:14.275 --> 00:10:16.942
My... My dad taught me,
and I taught Cam.

126
00:10:16.944 --> 00:10:18.711
- Your dad raced?
- Oh, hell, yeah.

127
00:10:18.913 --> 00:10:22.983
And then my cousins still race,
and my uncles did race.

128
00:10:25.019 --> 00:10:27.853
I... I think my... my mom
would've raced too if,

129
00:10:27.855 --> 00:10:32.192
if my dad had let her.
Some of my best memories are...

130
00:10:32.194 --> 00:10:33.161
are tied up with racing.

131
00:10:34.229 --> 00:10:36.161
When I was 12, my dad
wanted me to ride so bad,

132
00:10:36.163 --> 00:10:39.900
he took a seat and bolted it
into his race car.

133
00:10:40.768 --> 00:10:42.834
And he, uh... he didn't have

134
00:10:42.836 --> 00:10:44.537
a second crash helmet,
so he asked me to use

135
00:10:44.539 --> 00:10:48.374
my football helmet, and, uh,
we went around the track once,

136
00:10:48.376 --> 00:10:51.479
and by the end of that time,
I was sold. This was for me.

137
00:10:57.152 --> 00:10:59.887
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

138
00:11:01.789 --> 00:11:03.789
I'm gonna eat it.
I'm gonna eat it.

139
00:11:03.791 --> 00:11:05.192
You can have it.

140
00:11:22.445 --> 00:11:26.348
There you are,
I finally got her to calm down.

141
00:11:27.114 --> 00:11:28.216
She's getting so big.

142
00:11:31.286 --> 00:11:32.387
Please say something.

143
00:11:33.455 --> 00:11:35.123
- Like what?
- Anything.

144
00:11:35.357 --> 00:11:36.891
You haven't said a word
since you got home.

145
00:11:42.364 --> 00:11:43.865
I talked to Bob Linsky today.

146
00:11:45.568 --> 00:11:46.835
Why'd you talk to him?

147
00:11:47.901 --> 00:11:49.868
He offered me a job running
his service center.

148
00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.839
You know how much
extra money that would pay?

149
00:11:52.407 --> 00:11:53.975
Is that all you guys
talked about?

150
00:11:56.244 --> 00:11:57.512
He's entering a new car
next season.

151
00:11:58.513 --> 00:12:00.015
He wants me to drive it for him.

152
00:12:00.415 --> 00:12:02.150
- You already have a ride.
- I know.

153
00:12:04.219 --> 00:12:06.620
You're not thinking of taking
him up on his offer, are you?

154
00:12:06.622 --> 00:12:08.255
I don't know what I'm gonna do.

155
00:12:08.257 --> 00:12:09.323
Riding for your dad
is one thing,

156
00:12:09.325 --> 00:12:11.591
but riding for that
son of a bitch is dangerous,

157
00:12:11.593 --> 00:12:13.092
in more ways than one.

158
00:12:13.094 --> 00:12:14.861
I hate to think
what your dad would say.

159
00:12:14.863 --> 00:12:17.163
I don't care what he'd say.
This is my life

160
00:12:17.165 --> 00:12:19.365
we're talking about, Cindy,
not my father's.

161
00:12:19.367 --> 00:12:21.402
Great, now you made her cry.

162
00:12:21.404 --> 00:12:24.271
This is what I'm talking about.
We live in this lousy tin can,

163
00:12:24.273 --> 00:12:25.938
and we can't even
have a conversation

164
00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:26.941
without waking the baby.

165
00:12:27.977 --> 00:12:28.742
This tin can happens to be
your family's home.

166
00:12:28.744 --> 00:12:30.311
Look, what you want
me to do?

167
00:12:30.313 --> 00:12:32.048
You want me to be
a loser all my life?

168
00:12:34.417 --> 00:12:36.149
I want to win races.

169
00:12:36.151 --> 00:12:38.084
I want to be a champion,
but that's something

170
00:12:38.086 --> 00:12:40.019
I'll never be racing for my dad.

171
00:12:40.021 --> 00:12:41.322
Have you talked to him
about this?

172
00:12:43.326 --> 00:12:44.391
Look, it's bad enough riding
for someone else,

173
00:12:44.393 --> 00:12:47.294
but riding for Bob Linsky?
You know that won't fly

174
00:12:47.296 --> 00:12:49.897
with your dad.
He'll fire you, son or no son.

175
00:12:49.899 --> 00:12:52.166
- Big frigging deal.
- Cam, it is a big deal.

176
00:12:52.168 --> 00:12:54.203
We got a baby now.
What are we gonna do for money?

177
00:12:54.437 --> 00:12:56.370
I told you that if I drive
for Linsky,

178
00:12:56.372 --> 00:12:58.373
he said he'll give me a job
at his service center.

179
00:12:58.375 --> 00:13:00.041
I can't believe
you trust this guy.

180
00:13:48.624 --> 00:13:50.025
Hey, you.

181
00:13:51.994 --> 00:13:54.296
I wish I could get this
man to pay his bills.

182
00:13:59.403 --> 00:14:00.903
Dad, can I talk to you
for a minute?

183
00:14:02.105 --> 00:14:03.507
Sure. Pull up a chair.

184
00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.516
All right. What's on your mind?

185
00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.119
I don't want you take this
the wrong way,

186
00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:19.423
but I think it's time
I made a change.

187
00:14:22.392 --> 00:14:23.660
All right. Let's hear it.

188
00:14:26.263 --> 00:14:27.665
I'm not gonna race
for you anymore.

189
00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.300
What was that?
What did you just say?

190
00:14:32.302 --> 00:14:34.037
I'm not gonna drive
for you anymore.

191
00:14:34.672 --> 00:14:36.005
I've thought about it
a long time.

192
00:14:37.207 --> 00:14:38.208
There's no other way.

193
00:14:39.409 --> 00:14:42.379
Hell, I thought you liked
racing too much to give it up.

194
00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.418
I'm not giving up racing.

195
00:14:49.152 --> 00:14:52.423
Oh, now, son,
how you gonna pull that off?

196
00:14:53.156 --> 00:14:54.723
You know you don't have
the money for that.

197
00:14:54.725 --> 00:14:56.327
I accepted an offer
from Bob Linsky.

198
00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:01.463
- Linsky?
- Take it easy.

199
00:15:01.465 --> 00:15:03.164
- I know you don't like...
- "Don't like him"

200
00:15:03.166 --> 00:15:04.100
is an understatement.

201
00:15:05.101 --> 00:15:05.969
He's a snake. He's a...
He's a piece of shit.

202
00:15:06.637 --> 00:15:08.169
You get involved with
the likes of him,

203
00:15:08.171 --> 00:15:09.805
and I guarantee you'll get hurt.

204
00:15:09.807 --> 00:15:10.708
Please try to understand.

205
00:15:11.776 --> 00:15:12.708
- No, I understand perfectly.
- No! No, you don't.

206
00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:13.843
- Oh, yes, I do!
- With Linsky in my corner,

207
00:15:13.845 --> 00:15:16.178
I'm gonna be an instant
competitor for the championship.

208
00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.447
Championship means more
than your father?

209
00:15:18.449 --> 00:15:20.082
It means more than
your loyalties?

210
00:15:20.084 --> 00:15:21.652
It means more to you than
your blood?

211
00:15:22.186 --> 00:15:24.820
Now, I did not bring you up
that way.

212
00:15:24.822 --> 00:15:28.591
Believe me, not racing
for you is the hardest decision

213
00:15:28.593 --> 00:15:30.495
- I've ever had to make.
- Apparently not.

214
00:15:33.731 --> 00:15:35.733
Hold on. Ho... Ho... Hold on.

215
00:15:36.167 --> 00:15:37.201
You're fired.

216
00:15:42.674 --> 00:15:43.775
Fucking Linsky!

217
00:15:45.811 --> 00:15:48.479
Cindy, wait up! Hey!

218
00:15:48.746 --> 00:15:51.415
<i>Wait up! Cindy! Hey!</i>

219
00:15:54.085 --> 00:15:55.353
What did you want me to do?

220
00:15:58.256 --> 00:15:59.724
I know I should've
told you first, okay?

221
00:16:56.181 --> 00:16:58.685
How we doing, Sam?
I'll have a beer.

222
00:17:04.288 --> 00:17:06.291
Just trying to drown
my sorrows, that's all.

223
00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.365
You wanna tell me about it?

224
00:17:21.239 --> 00:17:24.141
That bad, huh? I hear ya.

225
00:17:36.823 --> 00:17:37.857
You wanna give me a hint?

226
00:17:39.826 --> 00:17:41.394
I'll take that as a no.

227
00:17:42.862 --> 00:17:46.866
Hey, I got an idea.
Why don't you and me go fishing?

228
00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:49.601
Shit, we haven't been
fishing in years.

229
00:17:50.736 --> 00:17:52.270
Come on,
it'll make you feel better.

230
00:17:52.537 --> 00:17:54.237
I'll pick you up early
in the morning.

231
00:17:54.239 --> 00:17:55.908
We'll go down to
our fishing hole.

232
00:17:56.976 --> 00:17:58.711
Come on, it'll just be
like old times.

233
00:18:02.749 --> 00:18:06.219
So, if it ain't the great
Sam "The Man" Munroe.

234
00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.889
Fuck you, Jack. I ain't signing
no autographs tonight.

235
00:18:11.891 --> 00:18:13.258
Autograph?

236
00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:16.426
It's been a long time
since you were somebody.

237
00:18:16.428 --> 00:18:18.796
Hey, can't you see
the man wants to be left alone?

238
00:18:18.798 --> 00:18:21.231
What's it been, Sam?
Five, six years

239
00:18:21.233 --> 00:18:22.468
since you ever won a race?

240
00:18:23.803 --> 00:18:25.271
Don't push it, Jack.

241
00:18:25.471 --> 00:18:29.473
- No, no. Let him.
- Hey...

242
00:18:29.475 --> 00:18:31.375
- Let him.
- We always got next year.

243
00:18:31.377 --> 00:18:32.278
Mm-hm.

244
00:18:33.513 --> 00:18:36.181
You may finish in the top ten.
Hell, you may even win a race,

245
00:18:37.784 --> 00:18:39.684
but I doubt it.
What am I thinking?

246
00:18:39.686 --> 00:18:41.788
Not in that shitty equipment
that you got.

247
00:18:42.255 --> 00:18:46.592
But hey, don't take
my word for it. Ask your son.

248
00:19:11.952 --> 00:19:13.721
I told him not to push.

249
00:19:17.324 --> 00:19:18.826
He thinks it's all about
equipment.

250
00:19:20.828 --> 00:19:23.396
I'm gonna prove to him
I'm still the better driver.

251
00:19:25.899 --> 00:19:28.301
- Watch your step.
- He thinks I'm nothing.

252
00:19:30.804 --> 00:19:33.807
I'm a good man.
He'll remember it when I die.

253
00:19:34.307 --> 00:19:35.743
He'll remember
that I'm a good man.

254
00:19:36.043 --> 00:19:37.745
He knows you're
a good man now.

255
00:19:38.045 --> 00:19:40.514
No, he don't.
He... No, he don't.

256
00:19:51.859 --> 00:19:54.260
All right.
End of the line.

257
00:19:55.929 --> 00:19:59.664
Home sweet home. You ready?

258
00:20:02.937 --> 00:20:04.736
You sure cold cocked him.

259
00:20:04.738 --> 00:20:08.042
All right.
Watch your step.

260
00:20:11.879 --> 00:20:15.315
Right here in this rocker here.
Here we go.

261
00:20:18.485 --> 00:20:21.622
You gonna be all right? Okay.

262
00:20:24.458 --> 00:20:25.758
Night, killer.

263
00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:29.964
Oh, God.

264
00:20:40.074 --> 00:20:41.075
Sam?

265
00:20:43.978 --> 00:20:45.013
Sam?

266
00:20:47.048 --> 00:20:50.451
Hey! I gotta be dreaming.

267
00:20:52.787 --> 00:20:54.053
How are you?

268
00:20:54.055 --> 00:20:57.026
- I'm good.
- What time is it?

269
00:20:59.526 --> 00:21:00.962
What happened to your hand?

270
00:21:03.064 --> 00:21:05.800
- Jack Dunn.
- Who is Jack Dunn?

271
00:21:06.568 --> 00:21:08.002
That's a good question.

272
00:21:09.904 --> 00:21:12.505
- You know this looks pretty bad.
- Oh, hell, it's fine.

273
00:21:12.507 --> 00:21:13.741
I just need some aspirin.

274
00:21:14.475 --> 00:21:16.010
I drank too much last night.

275
00:21:17.846 --> 00:21:20.883
Well, I need to get you inside.
I want to put some ice on this.

276
00:21:21.817 --> 00:21:24.052
Well, that's mighty
neighborly of you.

277
00:21:25.086 --> 00:21:27.722
Oh. Come on in.

278
00:21:33.695 --> 00:21:36.596
- Welcome.
- Let me bandage this.

279
00:21:36.598 --> 00:21:38.733
- Got any Band-Aids?
- In the garage.

280
00:23:00.549 --> 00:23:02.484
Please don't do that.

281
00:23:04.186 --> 00:23:06.488
I'm sorry I was just
taking a look.

282
00:23:06.755 --> 00:23:09.192
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have
snapped at you.

283
00:23:10.926 --> 00:23:14.798
Don't worry about it.
Is this a '70?

284
00:23:15.531 --> 00:23:17.533
I'm impressed,
How'd you know that?

285
00:23:17.734 --> 00:23:20.670
Growing up, my dad
always had Mustangs.

286
00:23:21.204 --> 00:23:22.138
How long have you had it?

287
00:23:26.075 --> 00:23:29.678
- A long time.
- Does it run?

288
00:23:40.724 --> 00:23:41.858
Been a while.

289
00:24:04.681 --> 00:24:05.815
Oh, boy!

290
00:24:39.149 --> 00:24:40.648
Running like shit.

291
00:24:40.650 --> 00:24:42.683
That would be
that big God damn boat

292
00:24:42.685 --> 00:24:45.555
